  message: "Fixed in PR #2347, sub-point by sub-point, on dev 49bc5c6e4. (1) openapi: an openapi.yaml alone now yields 3 operation nodes (yaml:openapi.yaml:7-9:listPets:function, discovery_language yaml, 0 violations); alertmanager 9, koel 40. Language slots: phoenix stand-ins are elixir:... with discovery_language elixir (fixture); id_format 0 on eight repositories; the ipc linker was not re-run by me on dev (its tests ran in the suite). (2) ids held by two nodes: koel 0 (filed 1,445), workadventure 0 (filed 10), hocuspocus 0, openzeppelin 0; the hocuspocus 12 and openzeppelin 1 did not reproduce on the base commit either. A new validator check, node_id_uniqueness, makes a shared id an error. Over 42 repositories 617 -> 3; the 3 left are filed as WI-hugir-kubuk-ripig-fotuv-viviv-komir-kusis-hovil. (3) containment: koel 2,315 of 2,315 Vue directive nodes and workadventure 966 of 966 Svelte event nodes have a contains edge from their file. (4) di_resolution keeps the highest-confidence binding (test_linker_hash_seed_order.py); it has NO measured effect on a real repository, because the linker's method index reads a key no analyzer writes: filed as WI-lumip-girom-polib-labum-limom-ripon-zopog-gugud. (5) ruby_ffi: each registration resolves in its own C file (same test); these edges are self-loops the map drops (WI-judov, open). (6) napi: five files registering one name give the same 5 edges under six hash seeds (WI-rumuv, closed with this). (7) message_dispatch stand-ins carry their role in the name and slot (972 stand-in ids moved over 42 repositories, scheme v18). (8) tcl: 'util::helper 1' with util::helper declared resolves to tcl:src/n.tcl:2-4:helper:function. (9) starlark's run id is uuid:<...>. (10) import targets: proto, thrift and make includes end on the in-tree file node or on an external stand-in that is a node (fixture; capnp and requirements by their tests, not re-run live); the component linker runs on Svelte-only and Astro-only trees (test_component_linker_activation.py). (11) metabase bin: the 34 nodes in *.bb files are all clojure. Leftovers found on the way are filed: WI-honit-surof-pitok-bijiz-jubah-raguz-fobuz-jiboz (linkers), WI-lukid-romub-dodil-pogul-kuhah-donod-buvag-hifob (import targets), WI-mukir-zojok-jigag-komiv-hanas-jodot-povaf-bugul (script reachability), WI-saliz-mokik-ramap-gutit-mamij-dofuv-zovud-julin (symbol gaps). Outputs: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/idfive_11232026/closure/ (fixtures*.txt, trees_summary.txt, pair_check_dev.txt)."  # 9073
